{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["[I divined — <b>an expression of sign, omen</b>.]" "<b>I divined.</b> He had terafim, and because of that he would go toward serpents." "<b>I divined and He blessed me.</b> Rashi explained: when you came here, he had no sons, as it is written, 'ורחל בתו' etc. The Sages said: this leaves an opening for a disputant to argue and say that sons were born to Laban before Jacob's arrival; and what is written, 'for she is a shepherd' — and not they — that is because they were still small, one or two years old."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:46.914783185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}